mode: "100644"
text: "# Keyword Research & Technique\n\nHow to find the terms people actually search, how to place them, and how to build evergreen topical\nauthority — honestly (no fabricated volumes).\n\n> Re-verify tool/feature specifics quarterly.\n\n## Finding social keywords (use real demand, never invent it)\n\nSocial keyword research is different from Google SEO research — in-app engines rank short, visual\ncontent by **engagement, freshness, and the language inside the post**, and people search in\n**natural, spoken language.** Sources, best first:\n\n- **Platform autocomplete** — start typing a seed (\"vegan meal prep for…\") and the suggestions ARE\n  real queries. The single most reliable, free source.\n- **\"Others searched for\" / related searches** — the carousel on results pages (esp. TikTok) and\n  related-search chips reveal adjacent intent.\n- **The search-results page itself** — what already ranks shows the intent and the bar to beat.\n- **Comments & DMs** — questions people ask = queries to answer.\n- **Audience language** — from `audience-research`: the exact words your audience uses (not industry\n  jargon).\n- **Native search analytics** — YouTube (\"traffic source: search\" + the search terms), TikTok/IG\n  search insights show what found you. The user pulls these.\n- **Tools (optional)** — TikTok Creative Center, TubeBuddy/VidIQ (YouTube), Google Trends/Keyword\n  Planner for cross-platform demand.\n\n> **Honesty rule.** The agent **cannot pull live in-app search volumes.** Never state precise volume\n> numbers as fact. Give the user the *method* (autocomplete, related, native analytics, tools) and\n> work from the qualitative signal — relative interest, intent, specificity — not invented figures.\n\n**Prioritize** long-tail, intent-rich, *specific* queries (lower competition, higher intent) over\nbroad head terms — and queries that match what you can genuinely answer.\n\n## The on-content technique — lead with keywords, support with hashtags\n\nThe core move: **write for the search bar first, the hashtag second.** \"Hashtags categorize; keywords\nget you found.\"\n\n- **State the primary keyword in plain language, early and once or twice** — in the caption/title, not\n  buried. One clear search intent per post.\n- **The triple mention (video):** the same primary phrase in **(1) spoken audio** (say it in the first\n  few seconds — it gets transcribed), **(2) on-screen text** (a keyword headline, not decoration), and\n  **(3) the caption/description.** Align every signal to one intent so the algorithm is certain what\n  you're about.\n- **Then add 3–5 niche hashtags** (per platform caps) as category signals → `hashtag-strategy`.\n- **Descriptive over clever in search contexts** — but keep the hook for the feed (see the tension\n  below).\n\n## Don't keyword-stuff\n\nIn-app engines **reward natural language and penalize spam.** Cramming 20–30 keywords/hashtags signals\nspam, **dilutes your topical signal** (the algorithm can't tell what you're about), and tanks\nreadability. Write something a human wants to read; make sure the primary keyword appears **clearly,\nonce or twice.** Decorative on-screen text that hurts readability also backfires.\n\n## The search-vs-feed tension (resolve it, don't ignore it)\n\nSearch rewards **clarity** (\"Best Budget Mic for Podcasting 2026\"); the feed rewards an **intriguing\nhook**. They can conflict. Resolve by: leading the **title/first line clear and keyword-true**, then\nadding intrigue *after* the keyword; or letting the **on-screen hook** carry curiosity while the\n**caption/title** carries the keyword. Don't sacrifice the searchable phrase for a clever-but-vague\nline — or you win the scroll and lose the search.\n\n## Build topical clusters (evergreen authority)\n\nOne post rarely owns a query. **Cluster** content around a pillar topic — many posts answering the\nlong-tail questions around it — so the platform (and Google) see you as **the answer/authority** for\nthat topic. This:\n\n- mirrors the **niche topic authority** the growth skills rely on (search + recommendation overlap),\n- compounds: each evergreen post keeps surfacing and reinforces the others,\n- maps cleanly onto `content-pillars` → a pillar becomes a keyword cluster → many evergreen posts.\n\nFavor **evergreen, intent-answering** formats (how-tos, \"best X for Y\", explainers, comparisons) that\nstay searched — alongside, not instead of, timely feed content.\n\n## Measure (honestly)\n\nTrack **discoverability** signals, not vanity: impressions **from search**, search terms that found\nyou, profile visits from non-followers, saves, and follower growth from **evergreen** posts — via\nnative platform search analytics (+ Google Search Console / UTMs for off-platform). **WoopSocial\ndoes not break metrics out by search term** — it publishes the optimized content (caption, alt text\nwhere supported); the search read-out comes from the platforms.\n"
